            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-44973",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Billy is an interface filesystem abstraction for Go. Prior to 5.9.0, m ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Billy is an interface filesystem abstraction for Go. Prior to 5.9.0, multiple path traversal issues exist across different components of go-billy. Insufficient path sanitization and boundary enforcement may allow crafted paths (e.g., using ..) to escape intended base directories. While go-billy was not originally designed to provide a strong security boundary, some of these issues were inconsistent across some of the built-in implementations. This results in scenarios where applications relying on go-billy for some level of isolation may inadvertently expose access to unintended filesystem locations. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.9.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44973",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-44973\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/go-git/go-billy/v5\nFixed Version: 5.9.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-44973](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44973)\nBilly is an interface filesystem abstraction for Go. Prior to 5.9.0, multiple path traversal issues exist across different components of go-billy. Insufficient path sanitization and boundary enforcement may allow crafted paths (e.g., using ..) to escape intended base directories. While go-billy was not originally designed to provide a strong security boundary, some of these issues were inconsistent across some of the built-in implementations. This results in scenarios where applications relying on go-billy for some level of isolation may inadvertently expose access to unintended filesystem locations. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.9.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-44973**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/go-git/go-billy/v5|5.9.0|[CVE-2026-44973](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44973)|\n\nBilly is an interface filesystem abstraction for Go. Prior to 5.9.0, multiple path traversal issues exist across different components of go-billy. Insufficient path sanitization and boundary enforcement may allow crafted paths (e.g., using ..) to escape intended base directories. While go-billy was not originally designed to provide a strong security boundary, some of these issues were inconsistent across some of the built-in implementations. This results in scenarios where applications relying on go-billy for some level of isolation may inadvertently expose access to unintended filesystem locations. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.9.0."
              },
